---
import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';
import CopyButton from '../../components/CopyButton.astro';
import { authoredBlogMetadata, formatBlogDate } from '../../data/blogPresentation';
import {
  createBreadcrumbSchema,
  createSoftwareApplicationSchema,
  productFacts,
} from '../../data/productFacts';
import { agenticFacts, agentPromptLibrary } from '../../data/agenticFacts';

const pageUrl = new URL('blog/localcloud-for-ai-agents/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString();
const metadata = authoredBlogMetadata['localcloud-for-ai-agents'];
const publishDate = metadata.publishedAt;
const contents = [
  { id: 'agent-prompt', label: 'Agent prompt' },
  { id: 'sandbox', label: 'A safe local sandbox' },
  { id: 'agent-entry', label: 'The agent entry point' },
  { id: 'local-loop', label: 'The local loop' },
  { id: 'safety', label: 'Validation boundaries' },
];
const quickstartPrompt = agentPromptLibrary.find((prompt) => prompt.id === 'quickstart')?.prompt ?? '';
const quickStart = agenticFacts.cliQuickStart;
const startCommands = quickStart.lines.slice(0, quickStart.lines.indexOf(quickStart.readiness));

const structuredData = [
  createSoftwareApplicationSchema(
    pageUrl,
    'LocalCloud gives AI coding agents a safe local Google Cloud target: Docker runtime, localhost SDK endpoints, raw Markdown instructions, Agent Skills, and MCP tooling boundaries.',
  ),
  createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: productFacts.siteUrl },
    { name: 'Blog', url: new URL('blog/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString() },
    { name: 'LocalCloud for AI Agents', url: pageUrl },
  ]),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'LocalCloud for AI Agents',
    datePublished: publishDate,
    dateModified: publishDate,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'LocalCloud' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'LocalCloud' },
    mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
    description: 'How LocalCloud turns local Google Cloud development into an agent-safe workflow with no default GCP credentials and explicit production validation boundaries.',
  },
];
---

<BlogLayout
  title="Introducing LocalCloud for AI Coding Agents (July 2026)"
  description="July 2026 announcement: LocalCloud gives coding agents a local Google Cloud sandbox with localhost SDK endpoints, Markdown instructions, and Agent Skills."
  structuredData={structuredData}
  {contents}
>
  <Fragment slot="hero">
  <article class="site-section site-section--hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow reveal">
      <nav class="mb-5 text-sm text-[var(--text-2)]" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></nav>
      <span class="site-eyebrow"><span class="site-eyebrow__pulse"></span>LocalCloud Blog</span>
      <h1 class="mt-5">LocalCloud for AI Agents</h1>
      <p class="blog-meta"><span>Published <time datetime={publishDate}>{formatBlogDate(publishDate)}</time></span><span>{metadata.minutes} min read</span><span>{metadata.topic}</span></p>
      <p class="blog-deck">
        Coding agents are good at writing integration code. Cloud credentials are the dangerous part. LocalCloud gives those agents a local Google Cloud target they can use by default: one Docker container, standard SDKs pointed at localhost, and explicit instructions to stop instead of falling back to real Google Cloud.
      </p>
      <div class="blog-actions">
        <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href="/ai/agents.md">Open /ai/agents.md</a>
        <a href="/ai/">AI agent guide</a>
        <a href="/compatibility/">Compatibility</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="site-section site-section--tight">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="site-panel p-6 reveal">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
          <div><span class="site-kicker">The prompt</span><h2 class="mt-3" id="agent-prompt">Give this to an agent</h2></div>
          <CopyButton text={quickstartPrompt} analyticsLabel="copy-blog-ai-agent-prompt" />
        </div>
        <pre class="blog-prompt"><code>{quickstartPrompt}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-section">
    <div class="container container--narrow space-y-10">
      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">Problem</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3" id="sandbox">Agents need a sandbox, not your cloud account</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          A repo that uses BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Firestore, Cloud Storage, Spanner, Bigtable, or Terraform often expects a real GCP project. If an agent follows that path blindly, a local test can become a credential request, a billing event, or a mutation against shared infrastructure.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          LocalCloud changes the default. The agent starts a local runtime, exports emulator environment variables, and proves one narrow SDK or Terraform path against localhost. Production validation still happens later, deliberately, against real Google Cloud after emulator variables are removed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">What changed</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3" id="agent-entry">A canonical agent entry point</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          The agent-facing entry point is <a href="/ai/agents.md">/ai/agents.md</a>. It is raw Markdown so coding agents can fetch it without parsing a rendered page. The human companion page is <a href="/ai/">/ai/</a>, which explains the workflow, copy prompts, service matrix, safety boundaries, AGENTS.md template, Agent Skills package, and raw Markdown resource index.
        </p>
        <ul class="site-list mt-5">
          <li><a href="/ai/services.md">/ai/services.md</a> gives agents the service matrix and endpoint variables.</li>
          <li><a href="/ai/compatibility.md">/ai/compatibility.md</a> lists what each service runs locally and where its local behavior stops.</li>
          <li><a href="/ai/docs.md">/ai/docs.md</a> points agents to SDK, Terraform, seed data, and console docs.</li>
          <li><a href={productFacts.agentSkillsUrl}>Agent Skills</a> provide portable workflows for BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Terraform, internal automation, seed data, and SDK tests.</li>
          <li><a href="/glossary/mcp-server/">LocalCloud MCP integration</a> provides structured tools and prompts through the runtime’s canonical <code>/mcp</code> endpoint and the <code>localcloud mcp</code> stdio bridge.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">How it works</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3" id="local-loop">One local loop agents can execute</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>1. Install and start LocalCloud</h3>
            <pre class="mt-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs"><code>{startCommands.join('\n')}</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>2. Verify readiness</h3>
            <pre class="mt-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs"><code>{quickStart.readiness}</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>3. Export localhost SDK endpoints</h3>
            <pre class="mt-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs"><code>{agenticFacts.envExportCommand}</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>4. Run the smallest local proof</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Create one dataset, topic, bucket, document, or table through the same SDK path the project uses. If a feature is unsupported locally, document the gap instead of using real GCP as a fallback.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">Safety model</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3" id="safety">The boundaries are part of the product</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          Agents follow one short list of direct rules, published in <a href="/ai/agents.md">/ai/agents.md</a>: use only local endpoint values, stop instead of reaching for real credentials or real Google Cloud, and validate against real Google Cloud before production.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          The proprietary Public Preview License permits individuals and organizations, including for-profit companies, to use LocalCloud for non-production development, testing, CI, evaluation, and internal pilots. It is not a production Google Cloud replacement. Use the <a href="/services/">service catalog</a> and <a href="/compatibility/">compatibility page</a> before relying on a local result, then validate release behavior against real Google Cloud.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BlogLayout>
